  "baseline_fairness_verdict": {
    "core_resolution_alpha1_vs_alpha5": "Baseline alpha=5.0 achieves lower log loss on 2024 (1.7601 vs 1.8535) because it raises tail probability on 0-win grid slots, protecting against extreme upsets (Miami P5, Brazil P17). However, on 2025 (where 16/24 races were won from pole), Baseline alpha=1.0 outperforms alpha=5.0 (1.1325 vs 1.1766) because it places higher confidence on pole converters. Crucially, when the Hybrid Geometric formulation is constructed using Prior alpha=5.0, it achieves 1.6892 log loss on 2024 (beating Baseline alpha=5.0 by -0.0709) and 1.0359 on 2025 (beating Baseline alpha=5.0 by -0.1407). Thus, the hybrid improvement is GENUINE and holds against BOTH alpha=1.0 and alpha=5.0 baselines."
  }
